       A: Each resource type is converted to cost using standard internal tariffs (energy at plant average $/kWh, material at standard material cost $/kg, labour at loaded hourly rate $/hr); the denominator is total shift cost in $, making resource_efficiency equivalent to value delivered per dollar spent.
    2. resource_efficiency
       Q: Is there an upper bound on any individual resource consumption rate (e.g., peak power draw ≤ X kW, or shift energy budget ≤ Y kWh) to prevent the optimiser from substituting one cheap resource for a scarcer one in ways that appear efficient on the ratio but create operational or safety problems?
